What is Iterable ?

Ans :- Iterable is root interface for collections framework
     - It was introduced in Java 5
     - It is present in java.lang package.
     - Collection extends Iterable Interface, so all its subtypes inherit iteration capability.
     - ✅ Allows iteration using Iterator and for-each loop.

     Public class Iterator{
      List<String> Names = Arrays.asList("Anand", "Kulkarni", "Java");
      Names.forEach(name -> System.out.println(name));
      } // For Each loop Iteration.
